<title>CHINA: China personal income tax revenue up in Q1.</title>
<headline>China personal income tax revenue up in Q1.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>China's personal income tax revenue soared by 43.7 percent to 5.409 billion yuan ($651.7 million) in the first quarter of 1997 compared with the year-ago period, the China Taxation News said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The figure accounted for 22.5 percent of the target for the whole year, the newspaper said.</p>
<p>The top tax collectors were southern Guangdong province, Shanghai, Beijing, southeastern Fujian province and eastern Zhejiang province, it said. It gave no further details.</p>
<p>($1 = 8.3 yuan)</p>
<p>-- Beijing Newsroom (8610) 6532 1921</p>
</text>
